# LF everywhere, enforced at checkout. This is not cosmetic: the per-tool
# Content-Security-Policy pins the SHA-256 of each tool file's inline script,
# computed over the exact bytes in site/tool/. A Windows clone with
# core.autocrlf=true would materialise those files with CRLF, silently
# changing the hash the build computes away from the bytes already deployed —
# and the build's CRLF guard would (rightly) refuse to build at all.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.xlsx binary
*.docx binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.woff2 binary
